"Estimator and choose a dynamical decoupling sequence.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na code cell ay nagpapakita kung paano i-enable ang dynamical "
"decoupling para sa Estimator at pumili ng isang dynamical decoupling "
"sequence.\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Twirling, also known as [randomized "
"compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325),"
" is a widely used technique for converting arbitrary noise channels into "
"noise channels with more specific structure.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang twirling, na kilala rin bilang [randomized "
"compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325),"
" ay isang malawakang ginagamit na teknik para sa pag-convert ng mga "
"arbitrary na noise channel sa mga noise channel na may mas tiyak na "
"istraktura.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli twirling is a special kind of twirling that uses Pauli operations. It "
"has the effect of transforming any quantum channel into a Pauli channel. "
"Performed alone, it can mitigate coherent noise because coherent noise tends"
" to accumulate quadratically with the number of operations, whereas Pauli "
"noise accumulates linearly. Pauli twirling is often combined with other "
"error mitigation techniques that work better with Pauli noise than with "
"arbitrary noise.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Pauli twirling ay isang espesyal na uri ng twirling na gumagamit ng mga "
"Pauli operation. Mayroon itong epekto ng pag-transform ng anumang quantum "
"channel sa isang Pauli channel. Kapag ginawa nang mag-isa, maaari nitong "
"mapagaan ang coherent noise dahil ang coherent noise ay may tendency na mag-"
"accumulate nang quadratically kasabay ng bilang ng mga operasyon, "
"samantalang ang Pauli noise ay nag-a-accumulate nang linearly. Ang Pauli "
"twirling ay madalas na pinagsama sa iba pang mga teknik ng error mitigation "
"na mas gumagana sa Pauli noise kaysa sa arbitrary na noise.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli twirling is implemented by sandwiching a chosen set of gates with "
"randomly chosen single-qubit Pauli gates in such a way that the ideal effect"
" of the gate remains the same. The result is that a single circuit is "
"replaced with a random ensemble of circuits, all with the same ideal effect."
" When sampling the circuit, samples are drawn from multiple random "
"instances, rather than just a single one.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Pauli twirling ay isinasagawa sa pamamagitan ng pag-sandwich ng isang "
"piniling hanay ng mga gate gamit ang mga random na piniling single-qubit "
"Pauli gate sa paraang nananatiling pareho ang ideal na epekto ng gate. Ang "
"resulta ay ang isang circuit ay pinapalitan ng isang random na ensemble ng "
"mga circuit, lahat ay may parehong ideal na epekto. Kapag nagsa-sample ng "
"circuit, ang mga sample ay kinukuha mula sa maraming random na instance, "
"hindi lang sa iisa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Since most of the errors in current quantum hardware come from two-qubit "
"gates, this technique is often applied exclusively to (native) two-qubit "
"gates. The following diagram depicts some Pauli twirls for the CNOT and ECR "
"gates. Every circuit within a row has the same ideal effect.\n"
msgstr ""
"Dahil karamihan sa mga error sa kasalukuyang quantum hardware ay nagmumula "
"sa mga two-qubit gate, ang teknik na ito ay madalas na inilalapat nang "
"eksklusibo sa mga (native) two-qubit gate. Ang sumusunod na diagram ay "
"naglalarawan ng ilang Pauli twirl para sa mga CNOT at ECR gate. Ang bawat "
"circuit sa loob ng isang hilera ay may parehong ideal na epekto.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Pauli twirling can be enabled by setting `enable_gates` to `True` in the "
"[twirling options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-twirling-options). Other notable options include:\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring i-enable ang Pauli twirling sa pamamagitan ng pag-set ng "
"`enable_gates` sa `True` sa [mga opsyon ng "
"twirling](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-"
"twirling-options). Kasama sa iba pang kapansin-pansing mga opsyon ang:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`num_randomizations`: The number of circuit instances to draw from the "
"ensemble of twirled circuits.\n"
msgstr ""
"`num_randomizations`: Ang bilang ng mga circuit instance na kukuhanin mula "
"sa ensemble ng mga twirled circuit.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`shots_per_randomization`: The number of shots to sample from each circuit "
"instance.\n"
msgstr ""
"`shots_per_randomization`: Ang bilang ng shots na isa-sample mula sa bawat "
"circuit instance.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code cell shows how to enable Pauli twirling and set these "
"options for Estimator. None of these options are required to be set "
"explicitly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na code cell ay nagpapakita kung paano i-enable ang Pauli "
"twirling at i-set ang mga opsyong ito para sa estimator. Wala sa mga opsyong"
" ito ang kinakailangang i-set nang explicitly.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-"
"trex}"
msgstr ""
"Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-"
"trex}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mitigates the effect of measurement errors for the estimation of Pauli observable expectation values.\n"
"It is based on the notion of twirled measurements, which are accomplished by randomly substituting measurement gates by a sequence of (1) a Pauli X gate, (2) a measurement, and (3) classical bit flip. Just like in standard gate twirling, this sequence is equivalent to a plain measurement in the absence of noise, as depicted in the following diagram:\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang [Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) ay nagpapagaan ng epekto ng mga measurement error para sa pagtatantya ng mga expectation value ng Pauli observable.\n"
"Batay ito sa konsepto ng twirled measurements, na naaabot sa pamamagitan ng random na pagpapalit ng mga measurement gate ng isang sequence ng (1) isang Pauli X gate, (2) isang measurement, at (3) classical bit flip. Tulad ng sa standard gate twirling, ang sequence na ito ay katumbas ng isang simpleng measurement kung walang noise, tulad ng inilalarawan sa sumusunod na diagram:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the presence of readout error, measurement twirling has the effect of diagonalizing the readout-error transfer matrix, making it easy to invert. A rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel is learned by\n"
"benchmarking random circuits initialized in the zero state. This allows\n"
"the service to remove bias from expectation values that result from\n"
"readout noise. Estimating the readout-error transfer matrix requires executing additional calibration circuits, which introduces a small overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Sa presensya ng readout error, ang measurement twirling ay may epekto ng pag-diagonalize ng readout-error transfer matrix, na ginagawa itong madaling i-invert. Natututo ang isang rescaling term mula sa diagonal noise channel sa pamamagitan ng\n"
"benchmarking ng mga random na circuit na na-initialize sa zero state. Pinapayagan nito ang\n"
"serbisyo na alisin ang bias mula sa mga expectation value na nagmumula sa\n"
"readout noise. Ang pagtatantya ng readout-error transfer matrix ay nangangailangan ng pagpapatupad ng karagdagang mga calibration circuit, na nagdudulot ng maliit na overhead.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enable TREX by using the `measure_mitigation` option {#enable-trex-by-using-"
"the-measure-mitigation-option}"
msgstr ""
"I-enable ang TREX gamit ang opsyon na `measure_mitigation` {#enable-trex-by-"
"using-the-measure-mitigation-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"TREX can be enabled by setting `measure_mitigation` to `True` in the [Qiskit"
" Runtime resilience options](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-"
"runtime/options-resilience-options-v2) for Estimator. Options for "
"measurement noise learning are described "
"[here](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-measure-"
"noise-learning-options). As with gate twirling, you can set the number of "
"circuit randomizations and the number of shots per randomization.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaaring i-enable ang TREX sa pamamagitan ng pag-set ng `measure_mitigation`"
" sa `True` sa [mga opsyon ng Qiskit Runtime "
"resilience](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-"
"resilience-options-v2) para sa Estimator. Ang mga opsyon para sa measurement"
" noise learning ay inilalarawan "
"[dito](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-measure-"
"noise-learning-options). Tulad ng gate twirling, maaari mong i-set ang "
"bilang ng mga circuit randomization at ang bilang ng shots bawat "
"randomization.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The following code cell shows how to enable TREX and set these options for "
"Estimator. None of these options have to be set explicitly.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang sumusunod na code cell ay nagpapakita kung paano i-enable ang TREX at "
"i-set ang mga opsyong ito para sa Estimator. Wala sa mga opsyong ito ang "
"kinakailangang i-set nang explicitly.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enable TREX by using the `resilience_level` option {#enable-trex-by-using-"
"the-resilience-level-option}"
msgstr ""
"I-enable ang TREX gamit ang opsyon na `resilience_level` {#enable-trex-by-"
"using-the-resilience-level-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable TREX by setting the [resilience level](/guides/estimator-"
"noise-management#resilience) to `1`, as shown in the following example.\n"
msgstr ""
"Maaari mong i-enable ang TREX sa pamamagitan ng pag-set ng [resilience "
"level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) sa `1`, tulad ng "
"ipinapakita sa sumusunod na halimbawa.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating errors in "
"estimating expectation values of observables. While it often improves "
"results, it is not guaranteed to produce an unbiased result.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) ay isang teknik para mapagaan ang mga "
"error sa pagtatantya ng mga expectation value ng mga observable. Habang "
"madalas nitong pinapabuti ang mga resulta, hindi garantisado na makakagawa "
"ito ng walang bias na resulta.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE consists of two stages:\n"
msgstr "Ang ZNE ay binubuo ng dalawang yugto:\n"

#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple "
"times at different noise rates.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Noise amplification_: Ang orihinal na quantum circuit ay isinasagawa nang "
"maraming beses sa iba't ibang antas ng noise.\n"

#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"_Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy "
"expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr ""
"_Extrapolation_: Ang ideal na resulta ay tinatantya sa pamamagitan ng pag-"
"extrapolate ng mga maingay na resulta ng expectation value patungo sa zero-"
"noise limit.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in many different ways. Qiskit Runtime implements noise amplification by \"digital gate folding,\" which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^\\dagger U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. For the extrapolation, you can choose from one of several functional forms, including a linear fit or an exponential fit.\n"
"The image below depicts digital gate folding on the left, and the extrapolation procedure on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang parehong noise amplification at extrapolation na yugto ay maaaring ipatupad sa maraming iba't ibang paraan. Ang Qiskit Runtime ay nagpapatupad ng noise amplification sa pamamagitan ng \"digital gate folding,\" na nangangahulugang ang mga two-qubit gate ay pinapalitan ng mga katumbas na sequence ng gate at ang inverse nito. Halimbawa, ang pagpapalit ng isang unitary $U$ ng $U U^\\dagger U$ ay magbubunga ng noise amplification factor na 3. Para sa extrapolation, maaari kang pumili mula sa isa sa ilang functional form, kasama ang linear fit o exponential fit.\n"
"Ang larawan sa ibaba ay naglalarawan ng digital gate folding sa kaliwa, at ang extrapolation procedure sa kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr ""
"![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-"
"explanation/zne.avif)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The overhead of this method scales with the number of noise factors. The\n"
"default settings sample the expectation value at three noise factors,\n"
"leading to a roughly 3x overhead.\n"
msgstr ""
"Ang overhead ng pamamaraang ito ay nag-e-scale kasabay ng bilang ng mga noise factor. Ang\n"
"mga default na setting ay nagsa-sample ng expectation value sa tatlong noise factor,\n"
"na humahantong sa halos 3x na overhead.\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Enable ZNE by using the `zne_mitigation` option {#enable-zne-by-using-the-"
"zne-mitigation-option}"
msgstr ""
"I-enable ang ZNE gamit ang opsyon na `zne_mitigation` {#enable-zne-by-using-"
"the-zne-mitigation-option}"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
